configure: check the MIPS32 R5/R6 ISA level again

"OE-A: 0005-mips64-cpu-detection" (and skyjet18's 6.1 commit 26fa6ac2b1
"configure: fix mips64 cpu detection") remove the toolchain checks of
mips32r6 and mips32r5 together with the mips64r6 one. Without them both
stay enabled on every 32-bit MIPS build that does not pass
--disable-mips32r5/--disable-mips32r6, so with the FPU inline assembly
configure adds -mfp64 and every link against the FP32 C library fails
("linking -mfp64 module with previous -mfp32 modules"); configure then
reports libxml2 as missing and finally stops at "Building with assembly
enabled is not supported on platforms without aligned memory allocations".
Keep the mips64 change, restore the two mips32 checks.

--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -6731,6 +6731,10 @@ elif enabled mips; then

         disable mips32r6 && disable mips32r5 && disable mips32r2
     else
+        enabled mips32r6 && check_inline_asm mips32r6 '"aui $0, $0, 0"' &&
+            disable mips32r5 && disable mips32r2
+
+        enabled mips32r5 && check_inline_asm mips32r5 '"eretnc"'
         enabled mips32r2 && check_inline_asm mips32r2 '"ext $0, $0, 0, 1"'

         disable mips64r6 && disable mips64r5 && disable mips64r2
